Z||000000||wcapman||12-11-2001||09:13 PM||||Does anyone know where I can get Fiero belts rewebbed in black?  So far I have sent them to 2 different places and they were returned saying they didn't do Fieros.  It's the double winder.  I want to get them redone in black to match the interior.||||reg||1
Z||000001||PAUL88GT||12-12-2001||12:12 AM||||Hey, I don't know the answer to your question.  Why don't you dye them black.  That should cost a lot less. Just my $0.02.<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||camon||12-12-2001||01:11 AM||||Sounds like a descent idea....<P>The only problem I could see if dying them.... <P>Is if you get in the car and your shirt would be damp from rain or something their is a chance that the dye could transfer to your shirt.<P>Just a thought!<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||12-12-2001||09:33 AM||||Is there any dye that wouldnt transfer?  im trested in making a black interior...<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000004||wcapman||12-12-2001||10:35 AM||||What I have been advised is NOT to dye them.  I've read that it weakens the webbing and could cause them to fail.  Besides I tried dying them with RITZ dye.  I tried 1 package of black, it made them look dirty. Two packs of black, they looked dirtier.  Then I was told to use a pack of scarlet red and two packs of black.  Besides making a mess of my kitchen, they came out dirty grey/red.  I don't think that dying is the answer.  Grease and body oil on the webbing affect the uptake of the dye, and the nylon has been treated with stain resistant stuff like Scotchguard.  The plastic parts of the buckles dyed black nicely.    Still looking for a supplier of black webbing.  Someone suggested an aircraft supplier.   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||AnimalGT||12-12-2001||11:50 AM||||Try here: <A HREF="http://www.aircraftspruce.com" TARGET=_blank>www.aircraftspruce.com</A> <BR>They sell almost everything that aircraft homebuilders need.  They maybe able to help you.  <BR>Scott||||reg||1
